Hi,

(Resending this email through my personal ID. Currently as my org
email ID is not allowing mails to lists.openembedded.org )

We are cross testing rust using poky sdk for all targets,
However, we are seeing some limitations with x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu target.

The rust config.toml we are using is as follows,
============================
[target.armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf]
cxx    = "/build-sdk/tmp/work/armv7vet2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi/rust-test/1.46.0-r0/wrapper/target-rust-cxx"
cc      = "/build-sdk/tmp/work/armv7vet2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi/rust-test/1.46.0-r0/wrapper/target-rust-cc"
linker = "/build-sdk/tmp/work/armv7vet2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi/rust-test/1.46.0-r0/wrapper/target-rust-ccld"

[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]
cxx    = "/build-sdk/tmp/work/armv7vet2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi/rust-test/1.46.0-r0/wrapper/build-rust-cxx"
cc      = "/build-sdk/tmp/work/armv7vet2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi/rust-test/1.46.0-r0/wrapper/build-rust-cc"

[rust]
rpath = true
channel = "stable"
optimize = true
verbose-tests = true

[build]
submodules = false
docs = false
rustc = "/build-sdk/tmp/work/armv7vet2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi/rust-test/1.46.0-r0/rust-snapshot/bin/rustc"
cargo = "/build-sdk/tmp/work/armv7vet2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi/rust-test/1.46.0-r0/rust-snapshot/bin/cargo"
vendor = true
target = ["armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf"]
host = ["x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu"]
build = "x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu"
============================

Where "target-rust-cc" contains cross compilation command.
============================
#!/bin/sh
exec arm-poky-linux-gnueabi-gcc  -march=armv7ve -mthumb -mfpu=neon
-mfloat-abi=hard -fstack-protector-strong  -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2
-Wformat -Wformat-security -Werror=format-security
--sysroot=/build-sdk/tmp/work/armv7vet2hf-neon-poky-linux-gnueabi/rust-test/1.46.0-r0/recipe-sysroot
"$@"
============================

Where "build-rust-cc" contains native compilation command.
============================
#!/bin/sh
exec gcc  "$@"
============================

We change the  first "[target.armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf]" in
config.toml with respect target which we interested to test.

Test execution for cross target
export TEST_DEVICE_ADDR="127.0.0.1:12345"
python3 src/bootstrap/bootstrap.py build src/tools/remote-test-server
-vv  --target  "armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf"


In case of testing for  "x86_64" i.e., rust target "x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu"

1.  When the target and build section triplet are identical  getting
below error.
         error: failed to run custom build command for `memchr v2.3.3`

2.  If we rename target section as "target.x86_64-poky-linux-gnu" then
the "target-rust-cc" is not considered while building tests or
remote-test-server.

Attached the logs of both the cases and config.toml used.

Please let me know how we can considere "poky toolchain"  for rust
cross testing of x86_64 target.

Regards,
Vinay

